+# Changes
+
+## Round 1
+
+- Added `parseRanges(text, pageCount)` in `src/parse-ranges.mjs`.
+- Added `tests/parse-ranges.test.mjs` covering the task examples, boundaries,
+  every TypeError and RangeError case in the checklist, and the choices below.
+- Documented `parseRanges` in `README.md` beside `paperSize`.
+
+Choices where the task was silent:
+- Result is de-duplicated and ascending ("1-3,2" gives `[1, 2, 3]`).
+- Spaces around parts and around the dash are accepted.
+- Empty text, empty parts ("1,,2"), and backwards ranges ("5-3") throw `RangeError`.
+
+Findings addressed: none (first round).
+
+## Round 2
+
+Addresses every finding in REVIEW.md (held-out suite: 18 of 70 failed).
+`src/parse-ranges.mjs`, `tests/parse-ranges.test.mjs` and `README.md` now agree.
+
+- Order and repeats: pages come back in the order typed, and a page typed twice
+  comes back twice (no sort, no de-duplication). Findings: Order, Repeats.
+- Backward ranges: `"5-3"` is `[5, 4, 3]` instead of a RangeError. Finding: Backward.
+- Open ends: a missing first page means 1, a missing last page means the last
+  page (`"-3"`, `"8-"`, `"10-"`, `"-1"`). A lone `-` and ends past the document
+  (`"12-"`, `"-12"`) still throw RangeError. Finding: Open end.
+- Empty box: `""` or only spaces returns every page instead of throwing.
+  Empty parts (`"1,,2"`, `"1,"`, `",1"`) still throw. Finding: Empty.
+- Tests: replaced the earlier sort/dedupe, backward, open-end and empty-text
+  tests with the cases quoted in REVIEW.md; added refusal cases (`"12-8"`,
+  `"12-"`, `"-12"`, `"-"`, `"1 0"`, `"00"`) and a fresh-array-per-call check.
+- README: updated the `parseRanges` section to describe the above.
+- Checklist items 1-6 were already satisfied and remain so.
